SUMMARY:Fine-Tune Your First Open Source Model in 30 Minutes: A Live Walkt
 hrough
DESCRIPTION:All Things Open RTP Meetup\nSave the date now for our in-perso
 n September meetup!\n\nThe featured topic is wildly interesting and sure t
 o educate and entertain - **"Fine-Tune Your First Open Source Model in 30 
 Minutes: A Live Walkthrough"**.\n\nAnd good news.. we just added two new s
 peakers!\n\n**Becky Brown**\, Global Program Manager at SAS\, will deliver
  a 10-15 minute session titled "Beyond the Code: The Relationship Advantag
 e"\, and **Pat Clark**\, Ambassador for **[Randstad Digital powered by Tor
 c](https://www.torc.dev/community-ato?utm_source=atonewsletter&utm_medium=
 email&utm_campaign=atopartnership)\,** will briefly discuss the Torc commu
 nity\, jobs\, and ways to get involved.\n\nDoors open at 6:00 pm for netwo
 rking\, food and beverages\, and tons of (free) swag. Live programming beg
 ins at 6:30 sharp.\n\n**This meetup is sponsored and made possible by the 
 team at [Randstad Digital powered by Torc](https://www.torc.dev/community-
 ato?utm_source=atonewsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=atopartnership)
 .** Randstad Digital powered by Torc is a global community for technology 
 professionals looking to grow their careers\, meet good people\, build new
  skills\, and stay connected to opportunities along the way.\n\n* [Check o
 ut the website here](https://www.torc.dev/community-ato?utm_source=atonews
 letter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=atopartnership)\n* [Discord](http://t
 orc.dev/discord)\n* [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/torcdotdev
 /)\n* Social handle (all platforms) - @torcdotdev\n* Community Email - [[c
 ommunity@torc.dev](mailto:community@torc.dev)]([mailto:community@torc.dev]
 (http://mailto:community@torc.dev/) "[mailto:community@torc.dev](http://ma
 ilto:community@torc.dev/)")\n* Primary contact - Taylor\, VP of Global Com
 munity\n* Additional team contact - Briana\, Head of Global Operations\n\n
 **Date:** Tuesday evening\, September 8\n\n**Featured Speaker:** Nihal Kau
 l\, Lead Software Engineer\, Revscale AI\n\n**Topic:** Fine-Tune Your Firs
 t Open Source Model in 30 Minutes: A Live Walkthrough\n\n**Abstract:**\nTh
 is 30-45 talk walks through fine tuning a small open source model on a rea
 l dataset\, live on stage\, using a free Google Colab GPU. The audience se
 es the full workflow from dataset prep through training to a working fine-
 tuned model. The best part.. Nihal shares the notebook with attendees so t
 hey can run it themselves after the session.\n\n**Introductory Speaker:** 
 Becky Brown\, Global Program Manager\, SAS\n\n**Bio:**\nBecky Brown is a t
 echnology industry veteran whose career spans nearly four decades in sales
 \, product marketing\, and enablement. Today\, she leads Social Selling pr
 ograms at SAS\, helping professionals expand their influence through meani
 ngful digital engagement. Becky challenges technical audiences to think be
 yond skills and certifications\, demonstrating how strong relationships\, 
 authentic communication\, and strategic networking can amplify both person
 al and professional success.\n\n**Talk Title:** Beyond the Code: The Relat
 ionship Advantage\n\n**Abstract:**\nBecky will explore why relationship-bu
 ilding remains one of the most valuable skills and how you can leverage it
 . She will give you practical insights for building authentic connections 
 that expand your influence and help you open doors (without feeling selfpr
 omotional). Attendees will leave with a fresh perspective on networking an
 d simple strategies they can put into practice immediately\, both online a
 nd in person.\n\n**Venue Location & Directions:**\nLocation: Fidelity Inve
 stments\, Durham\, NC\n[[https://goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6](https://go
 o.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6)]([https://goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6](http
 s://goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6))\nIf you enter “Select Dr\, Durham\, 
 NC” into your navigation it will take you to the parking lot access road
  and then just follow the signs to Visitor parking and then to the buildin
 g we will be meeting in. Once you have arrived at the Guest Parking area\,
  proceed to the large building on the left.\n\n**Parking:** [[https://goo.
 gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6](https://goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6)]([https:
 //goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6](https://goo.gl/maps/VGu89aYsn8qt5xqa6))\n
 \n**Registration and Government ID Required**\nPlease note\, security prot
 ocols onsite require everyone attending to register ahead of time using yo
 ur first and last name as it appears on your government ID. **\\*Note\, by
  RSVP'ing for this meetup on [[Meetup.com](http://meetup.com/)]([http://me
 etup.com/](http://meetup.com/)) you are "registering" for the event.**\n\n
 **You'll need to bring that ID with you to the event.**\nUpon entry you wi
 ll be directed to a table where your id will be checked and you will be gi
 ven your pre-registered nametag and you will be escorted into the event sp
 ace. This will help speed you through the lobby and get you to the food\, 
 swag\, and content without delay.\n\n**Questions?** Contact us at [info@al
 lthingsopen.org.](http://info@allthingsopen.org./)\n\n**RSVP required**\n\
 \*This is a free event. However\, an RSVP is required. Seating is limited\
 , so RSVP's will be capped as we fill up. Please move quickly and RSVP to 
 save your spot if interested. When you RSVP you will be added to our maili
 ng list to receive future event updates. You can unsubscribe at any time.
